        "comments": "The assembly daArnMont1.hap1.1 is based on 65x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated as part of the European Reference Genome Atlas (ERGA, https://www.erga-biodiversity.eu/) via the Biodiversity Genomics Europe project (BGE, https://biodiversitygenomics.eu/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Heterozygous structural variation was observed in the following regions: chromosome 1, 34.25 Mb to 62.8 Mb; chromosome 4, 25.6 Mb to 29.7 Mb; chromosome 6, 28.8 Mb to 46.3 Mb; chromosome 18; 10.4 Mb to 12.4 Mb and chromosome 19, 14.3 Mb to 21.9 Mb.",
